text:
Iris: quick idea — instead of ad-hoc applies, we should produce an immutable apply_plan (snapshot_id + hash) that the console shows and the router/quota services all reference. prevents drift between what UI shows and what actually ran.

Tom: how do we handle concurrent modifies? CAS on snapshot_id + etag. if etag mismatch, apply fails with a clear reason and console shows diff vs current.

Anya: UX: side-by-side diff, highlight risky fields (billing/quota/route changes), and a small "simulate" action that runs the plan against a shadow router and returns a preview of routing fractions & estimated cost. also need a big red abort and a "safe-continue" that requires typing the snapshot_id.

Raj: telemetry/metrics: emit events `apply_plan.started` / `apply_plan.completed` / `apply_plan.rolled_back` with plan_id, stage_id, snapshot_hash. include per-stage metrics: request_count, p95_latency_ms, error_rate_pct, throttle_rate_pct. keep cardinality low by grouping cohorts into hashed buckets.

Sumi: ops concerns — require preflight checks: schema_compat, model_available, billing_quota_ok. If any preflight fails, mark plan `blocked` and surface exact failing check. Also require min_samples and a statistical test (e.g., 2-sample proportion z-test) before claiming a metric breach to avoid noisy rollbacks.

Iris: propose a compact proto-ish apply_plan schema (console + API agree):
```proto
message ApplyPlan {
  string plan_id = 1;
  string snapshot_id = 2;
  repeated Stage stages = 3;
  enum RollbackPolicy { AUTO = 0; MANUAL = 1; }
  RollbackPolicy rollback_policy = 4;
}
message Stage {
  int32 target_percent = 1;
  int32 duration_minutes = 2;
  repeated string checks = 3; // e.g., "p95<200"
  int32 min_samples = 4;
}
```

Tom: fallback strategies: `route_variant`, `quota_scale(0.5)`, or `split_to_stable`. make fallback pluggable and declared in the plan so apply logic is deterministic.

Anya: timeline UI: per-stage card with green/yellow/red state, a live events feed (last 100 events), and a small link to "inspect cohort traces" (opens trace query). keyboard accessibility + screenreader labels are required.

Raj: sampling guidance — for the affected cohorts bump trace sampling to 100% for first N minutes (configurable) then decay. Also record an aggregated `apply_signal` timeseries so SRE can quickly see if plan moved metrics.

Sumi: implementation flow: 1) console creates plan & does preflight checks; 2) snapshot + plan persisted (immutable); 3) apply queue orchestrates staged operations -> router / quota / billing adapters; 4) each adapter writes idempotent status event referencing plan_id & stage_id; 5) failure triggers rollback according to plan. Make all adapters emit `apply_status` to the event bus.

Iris: dependency-check idea — extend preflight to call `dependency_matrix` (model availability, infra capacity, team opt-in) and annotate plan with blockers so product/ops can resolve before apply.

Tom: audit trail — every plan write gets an immutable audit entry with actor, timestamp, snapshot_hash, and a human comment. we should also record `abort_reason` (metric_violation/manual/dependency).

Raj: dashboard work — add a small panel that shows active plans, per-plan health sparkline, and recent rollbacks. also attach a quick-query button to open logs/traces filtered by plan_id.

Sumi: CLI/API: support `--dry-run` flag that runs preflight + simulate step and returns predicted routing fractions + cost delta but does not change live state. Console should call this before final confirm.

deploy-bot: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/platform/pull/4620 — draft: apply_plan persistence, preflight checks, and event hooks. CI: ✅ unit, ⚠️ integration flaky on quota-sim.

Iris: next steps: I'll draft the RFC describing apply_plan schema, preflight matrix, and telemetry contract. volunteers: Tom (concurrency/CAS + adapters), Raj (telemetry/dashboard), Anya (console flows + accessibility), Sumi (ops/runbook). please ping if you can help with simulator runs.

Tom: I'll prototype CAS + etag flow and a small harness to emulate concurrent applies. aim to land proto + tests this week.

Raj: I'll sketch Grafana panels and a trace dashboard, and add the plan_id tag to our trace instrumentation plan.

Anya: will deliver the diff/simulate mocks and accessibility checklist by EOD tomorrow.

Sumi: thanks all — RFC incoming. we'll use this thread for quick followups. :thumbsup:
